Reading: odd-root motion b -> b+2 is the outer omega ladder;
row motion N -> 2N is the inner finite/omega ladder.  A proof that
discharges rows inside columns and then moves columns has omega^2 shape.
This is the precise infinite-game import: use ordinal rank to prevent
an infinite proof game from cycling through larger finite boards.

